text:
Yours. Facts for 'a federated or distributed trust, carried by the owner's key?'. The tree anchors all three on ONE key:
(1) the RELAY answers a signed status only to its owner ('is this key the owner here?', ownerBadge.js:5-9);
(2) the FACE obeys only the key in its puppet.json (ownerCommandIn, nodeApps.js:479-482);
(3) grantFace's answers reach members signed by the owner node.
So yes: one root key per group, and trust flows down by signed REPLIES, not certificates. No 'this face is mine' document exists that a member could show a third party; the member knows it only because the owner answered it. FEDERATED across owners: a member holding grants at several providers trusts several independent roots, and none vouches for another. Two consequences worth saying: losing the owner key loses the whole group (relay, face, grants); and revoking is the owner changing its own records (puppet.json, grants, the contact sync), with no revocation list to publish.
